.venv/
.certs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
assets/scenes/

# Never commit a real environment file; the repo is public.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Rendered walkthroughs. The app renders these itself (see docs/DEMO.md);
# a 210 MB master in git made the repo unpushable to GitHub, which caps a
# single file at 100 MB. They are build output, not source.
docs/*.mp4
# ...except the shareable cuts (2-14 MB each), which are well under GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file cap and are what the whitepaper, deck and wiki embed. The
# 210 MB master is what made this repository unpushable and stays out.
#
# Keep these small. A 14 MB pitch.mp4 failed to push with HTTP 408 -- a
# transfer timeout, not the size cap -- and the renderer now encodes the final
# concatenation at CRF 26 rather than 21, which halves it with no visible
# difference on static 1080p slides.
!docs/biodao-walkthrough.mp4
!docs/walkthrough-share.mp4
.keys/
!docs/pitch.mp4
!docs/investor.mp4
!docs/investor-web.mp4
!docs/investor-vertical.mp4
!docs/overview.mp4

# Generated repository analysis. `.enola/` is a tool's snapshot of this repo --
# an extractor cache, a facts dump and a rollover copy of the previous run,
# 3.3 MB of it. Every byte is derived from the source beside it and regenerated
# by re-running the tool, so committing it adds weight to every clone to
# preserve an answer that is stale the moment anything changes.
.enola/
